[00:21.10]1. We really want to imitate our God,
[00:25.56]To be impartial, as we know he is.
[00:30.68]To save all sorts of people is his will;
[00:35.40]He welcomes all to come and to be his.
[00:40.80](Chorus)
[00:41.22]It’s the person, not the place;
[00:43.36]It’s the heart and not the face.
[00:46.28]God’s message to all people we extend.
[00:50.86]So because we really care,
[00:53.58]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[00:55.88]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”
[01:09.52]2. It doesn’t matter where they may be found
[01:14.06]Or what at first they might appear to be.
[01:19.16]What really counts is what they are at heart—
[01:24.42]The inner self, the one Jehovah sees.
[01:29.38](Chorus)
[01:29.38]It’s the person, not the place;
[01:31.88]It’s the heart and not the face.
[01:35.00]God’s message to all people we extend.
[01:39.92]So because we really care,
[01:42.56]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[01:44.46]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”
[01:58.16]3. Jehovah welcomes all who make the choice
[02:02.58]To leave the world and all its ways behind.
[02:07.68]This we have learned, and this we want to share,
[02:12.68]And so we preach to people of all kinds.
[02:17.86](Chorus)
[02:17.92]It’s the person, not the place;
[02:20.46]It’s the heart and not the face.
[02:23.32]God’s message to all people we extend.
[02:28.50]So because we really care,
[02:31.08]We keep preaching ev’rywhere:
[02:32.90]“All sorts of people can become God’s friend.”
